.TH DEPLOY-OKD-PROXY 1 "August 2026" "mu2edaq-notify 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
deploy-okd-proxy.sh \- deploy the mu2edaq-pager OKD reverse proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/deploy-okd-proxy.sh
[\fB\-\-env\fR \fIprod\fR|\fItest\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR \fINAMESPACE\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIVALUES_FILE\fR]...
[\fB\-\-release\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-tls\-secret\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-cert\fR]
[\fB\-\-skip\-vault\fR]
[\fB\-\-vault\-approle\fR]
[\fB\-\-vault\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deploys the
.B mu2edaq-pager
Helm chart (see
.IR helm/ )
to an onsite OKD cluster: a Caddy container fronted by an OKD
.B Route
with edge TLS termination, forwarding to
.BR backend.url ,
normally the existing
.B mu2edaq-notify-server
running on the local Mu2e host. The Caddy image is built in-cluster (an
.B ImageStream
/
.B BuildConfig
derived from
.BR docker.io/library/caddy:2\-alpine ,
stripping a file capability the stock image carries that OKD's
.B restricted\-v2
SCC refuses to exec) \(en no external registry or local Docker build is
needed. This script does not touch
.B mu2edaq-notify-server
itself \(en it only stands up the public-facing proxy in front of it.
.PP
Because OKD rejects a
.B Route
that references a TLS secret before that secret exists, cert-manager
activation is a two-pass process (see
.BR docs/okd\-proxy\-operations.md ):
the script applies the Helm release once with
.B certManager.externalCertificate=false
to let cert-manager issue the certificate, waits for the resulting TLS
secret, then re-applies with
.B externalCertificate=true
to wire it into the Route. Pass
.B \-\-no\-cert
to skip this entirely and use the router's default wildcard certificate
instead, e.g. before the namespace has been allowlisted by the cluster's
OPA admission webhook for the target hostname.
.PP
Secrets normally come from Vault (see
.BR docs/Vault\-Secrets.md ),
but
.B SECRET_REGISTRY
in
.B scripts/vault_client.py
is empty today, so a bare
.B \-\-env
run still succeeds with no Vault login required.
.B my\-values.yaml
(gitignored) carries all of this deployment's real configuration \(en
hostname, cert-manager settings, and
.BR backend.url .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-env " prod|test"
Which Vault secrets instance to deploy with. Required unless
.B \-\-skip\-vault
is given.
.TP
.BI \-n " NAMESPACE"
OKD namespace (default: mu2edaq-pager). Created with
.B \-\-create\-namespace
if it doesn't already exist.
.TP
.BI \-f " VALUES_FILE"
Helm values file; repeat to layer files, later files win (default:
my\-values.yaml). Vault-sourced values are always applied last.
.TP
.BI \-\-release " NAME"
Helm release name (default: mu2edaq-pager).
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-secret " NAME"
cert-manager TLS secret name (default: mu2edaq-pager-tls). Overrides
.B certManager.secretName
so the wait loop and the Route's
.B externalCertificate
always agree.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SEC"
Timeout in seconds (default: 120), applied separately to each wait:
the TLS-secret wait, the image build, and the rollout.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cert
Skip cert-manager entirely; the Route uses the router's default
wildcard certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-vault
Deploy using only the
.B \-f
values files; don't call Vault at all
.RB ( \-\-env
is not required in this case).
.TP
.B \-\-vault\-approle
Authenticate to Vault as the application via
.BR get\-vault\-apptoken.sh (1)
instead of your personal
.IR ~/.vault\-token .
.TP
.BI \-\-vault\-role " ROLE"
AppRole role name to use with
.BR \-\-vault\-approle .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
First deploy, issuing a fresh cert-manager certificate:
.PP
.RS
.B ./scripts/deploy-okd-proxy.sh --env prod
.RE
.PP
Redeploy without touching cert-manager (route/cert already active):
.PP
.RS
.B ./scripts/deploy-okd-proxy.sh --env prod --no-cert
.RE
.PP
Deploy without any Vault call at all:
.PP
.RS
.B ./scripts/deploy-okd-proxy.sh --skip-vault
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B helm/
The mu2edaq-pager Helm chart.
.TP
.B my-values.yaml
Gitignored real deployment values (hostname, backend.url, cert-manager settings).
.TP
.B config/vault.yaml
Vault connection defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault\-client (1),
.BR get\-vault\-apptoken (1),
.B docs/okd-proxy-setup.md ,
.B docs/okd-proxy-operations.md ,
.B docs/Vault-Secrets.md
